>>__ Parse.temp_set_grammars $ valOf $ grammarDB {thyname="hol"};
## `aesop_ss`

``` hol4
aesopData.aesop_ss : unit -> simpExtLib.simpset
```

------------------------------------------------------------------------

Returns Aesop's simplifier default.

The base is `srw_ss ()`, lifted into the extension engine with
`simpExtLib.lift_simpset`; it is not the split-enabled `clasimp_ss ()`.
Derivation weakens conditional congruence, installs ETA matching, fixes
conditional depth at 40, and replaces both solver lists with Aesop's
selected safe and unsafe solvers. The additive `[aesop_simp]` rewrites are
then installed. Splitting remains the search engine's responsibility.

The result is derived from `srw_ss ()` when that changes; a change to the
`[aesop_simp]` rewrites alone is derived once more, keyed on the identity
of both inputs. Both follow `Context.restore`. Scope temporary changes to
the base with `BasicProvers.with_simpset_updates`.

